{
  "format": "coach_hire_fire_scenarios",
  "schema_version": 2,
  "purpose": "Shared hire/fire test cases for CoachesService (Unity) and any port. Same file, same expected results.",
  "constants": {
    "hire_cost_formula": "round(salary x 1,000,000 / 52)",
    "refund_rate": 0.5,
    "team_rating_baseline": 12,
    "team_rating_normalization": 1,
    "hire_source": "coach_hiring",
    "fire_refund_source": "coach_firing_refund"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Each scenario starts from input (coins and coaches_start) and applies steps in order. After every step, expected gives the result, wallet, the three coach slots, Team Rating and the events published by that step.",
    "Actions: hire (by coach_name; coach_id is the catalog id), fire (by role), set_games_served (test setup: sets games_served on the contract of the role, because the game does not increment it yet).",
    "A failed action (success false) changes nothing and publishes nothing. wallet_change is null when no coins move.",
    "Roles are O, D and ST. Event payloads use coach_type O, D and S (Special Teams is normalised to S by CoachesService).",
    "Team Rating = team_rating_baseline + sum of bonus_pct of the hired coaches, divided by team_rating_normalization. bonus_pct = round(average of the coach's 4 role stats x 5), taken from the coaches block.",
    "Wallet is coins only. Every list is explicit with named fields; no reader should rely on JSON key order.",
    "Expected values are calculated from the rules in CoachesService.cs, not copied from running the game."
  ],
